"],"val":["The price sits above its blended-model fair value of $56.79 (margin of safety -200%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 40%), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Consumer Cyclical peers: P/E 32.0 vs 17.7 and EV/EBITDA 29.0 vs 10.5 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 27% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an EBIT/EV of 2.8% (vs the 8% bar).","The 39 covering analysts target $205 on average, 21% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 1786% clears the cost of capital of 11.7% by 1774pp, the mark of a value creator.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.85x.","ROE of 31% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.7x equity multiplier).","It spends 19.2% of revenue on R&D and 13.0% on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $9.0B (9% of market cap)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 13.4% over 3 years.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 8%.","Capex runs only 0.6x depreciation (0.3% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.0%, and institutions hold 92%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (37 sales, net $46.5M sold).","It returns 3.7% a year to shareholders (3.7% in buybacks)."],"people":["With about 8,200 employees, each generates about $1.5M of revenue, 3.9x the Consumer Cyclical median, and revenue has grown 19.6% a year across its filed history.","The company is founder-led, which often keeps management aligned with long-term owners.","CEO pay is $242K (0x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (9/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $194K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":72,"head":"Avoid: priced 200% above its fair value of $56.79.","pros":["Composite 40, ab